  "TITLE": "Ecological Succession:<br>How Bare Ground<br>Becomes a Forest",
  "LEAD": "Clear a patch of land and it doesn't jump straight to forest &mdash; it goes through a predictable sequence, because each stage changes the conditions in a way that lets the next stage move in and outcompete it. Lichens and grasses tolerate bare, exposed soil that nothing else can, but the organic matter and shade they build up is exactly what shrubs need to take over next, and what shrubs build is what trees need after that. Each stage engineers itself out of a job.",
